        "Classify the harm and its incidence",
        "Activity abatement and defence are jointly chosen",
        "Assumptions and derivative notation",
        "Derive and interpret the efficient conditions",
        "Efficiency and the unpaid bill require different measures",
        "Why noise and air-pollution estimates can undercount",
        "Shortcuts and choice of a standard",
        "What valuation techniques measure",
        "Read the historical tables",
        "Accidents: risk valuation and aggregation",
        "What the review establishes",
        "Sources and page convention"
      ],
      "objective_ids": [
        "O008",
        "O009"
      ],
      "semantic_baseline": "Residual damage EC(Q,D,A); W=NPB−EC−A−D, NPB=PB−PC. Smooth interior maximum needs NPB_Q=EC_Q, EC_A=EC_D=−1 plus curvature/boundary checks; supplier/victim split has limits. Gross unpaid bill is EC+D with explicit outside-sector boundary; average total burden is not generally the marginal tax. Typology includes intra-sector, environmental and infrastructure effects, latter excluded from later review. Protection/abatement-only and damage valuations can omit components; surrogate/hypothetical markets versus physical-dose pricing differ in scope and uncertainty. Avoid overlap and stock/annual-flow mismatch. Historical tables and standard-sensitive estimates are not current causal truth; risk willingness-to-pay differs from earnings and accident aggregation/insurance boundaries matter.",
      "change_class": "new_content",
      "previous_path": null,
      "previous_hash": null,
      "affected_objective_ids": [
