        "Topic map and argument",
        "Seven principles for evaluating environmental policy",
        "Climate change: cooperation damage and uncertainty",
        "Energy production: price is incomplete without external costs",
        "Check the units in the numerical example",
        "Water: evaluate benefits and preserve uncertainty",
        "Lead service lines",
        "PFAS and cumulative exposure",
        "Wetlands and the WOTUS boundary",
        "Environmental federalism: match jurisdiction to the spillover",
        "Regulatory appraisal and discounting",
        "Deregulation counts are not a welfare measure",
        "Distribution research data and future capacity",
        "Conclusions recommendations and limits",
        "Sources and page convention"
      ],
      "objective_ids": [
        "O012"
      ],
      "semantic_baseline": "Seven principles cover market failure, complete accounting, discounting, uncertainty, distribution, jurisdiction and international cooperation. Early2025 conceptual critique uses cited cases, not original data/aggregate causal estimate; stages/dates retained. SCC vintage/discount choices are not current rate/CI; ton/MWh repairs power-unit mismatch and production-zero is not lifecycle-zero. Water benefits/cumulative PFAS exposure and legal-protection-versus-physical-loss boundaries matter. Local heterogeneity versus cross-border coordination is conditional. DiscountB/(1+r)^t considers timing of costs and benefits; deregulation counts are not welfare. R&D/information public goods and future capacity have forgone benefits; programme returns do not generalise automatically.",
