      ],
      "semantic_baseline": "Table 17.3 reports resubmission requests rising from 9% in 2007 to 48% in 2015, with fluctuations between those dates. Initial submission counts fall to 25 and 29 in 2014 and 2015, compared with 97 in each of 2012 and 2013. The series does not show a consistent disappearance of appraisal problems. The chapter's possible chilling effect of scrutiny on submissions is explicitly speculative; lower submissions alone do not establish its cause.* OECD chapter 17, PDF pp. 12–13 (printed pp. 434–435), Table 17.3",
