      ],
      "semantic_baseline": "Figure 13.2, physical p. 7, printed p. 209. Its letters belong to this figure, separately from Figure 13.1 and the lecture diagram.* Here $MNPB=MPB-MPC$ is marginal net private benefit in money per unit of activity $Q$, and $MEC$ is marginal external cost in the same units. The private choice $Q^0$ has $MNPB=0$; the social choice $Q^*$ has $MNPB=MEC=t^*$. The labelled areas integrate these marginal quantities and therefore measure money, rather than money per unit. Verhoef Externalities, physical PDF p. 7",
